["toddlers-1xbvw11","","professional","toddler_24_36_months","success_story",["bedtime_battle","consistency_failure","low_sleep_needs"],"The first night was a bit rough! He asked for one more book. I said no, it’s time for bed.","A sleep coach describes ending her own toddler's bedtime book negotiations over four nights."],
["toddlers-1xbvw11","","professional","toddler_24_36_months","belief",["bedtime_battle","consistency_failure","sleep_consultant"],"The funny part is that I’m actually a sleep coach, and I give this advice to parents all the time. […] But I fell into the exact same trap as so many of the parents I work with.","Sleep coach admits she let her own son's bedtime creep."],
["toddlers-1xbvw11","","professional","toddler_24_36_months","advice_given",["bedtime_battle","consistency_failure"],"It’s really normal, and it’s very insidious. At first you think, why not? But before you know it, bedtime is 15 or 20 minutes later than it should be.","How 'one more book' slides bedtime later."],
["toddlers-1xbvw11","19rg7rwvspco0","professional","toddler_24_36_months","pain",["low_sleep_needs","parent_identity"],"15-20 minutes when you only have like 1 hour of free time in the evening (if you want to get a full night sleep), is a lot!  My son only sleeps about 10 hours a day; it's rough having a low-sleep-needs toddler.","Why a 15-minute bedtime slide matters to her."],
["toddlers-1xbwboi","","parent_unspecified","toddler_12_24_months","pain",["night_wakings","short_naps","doctor"],"He wakes up from his nap so so miserable. Standing up in the crib, screaming, and will not calm until you hold him. He will snuggle and close his eyes for 20 minutes but never go back to sleep.","Sleep broke after a cold and ear infection; still waking after antibiotics."],
["toddlers-1xbwboi","","parent_unspecified","toddler_12_24_months","question",["night_wakings","doctor"],"I don’t know how to help him. He seems so miserable. Is this a sleep regression? Still uncomfortable?","Doctor says ears look better; sleep hasn't recovered."],
["sleeptrain-1xbwq0s","","partner","regression_4_months","pain",["wake_windows","short_naps","schedule_rigidity"],"I feel like all the advice on here assumes naps are predictable and consistent as well. Sometimes my kid naps for 20 minutes, sometimes for an hour.","Father building a schedule with his wife before Ferber at 4.75 months."],
["sleeptrain-1xbwq0s","","partner","regression_4_months","question",["short_naps","comparison_other_babies"],"Has anyone else dealt with this, or are other babies perfect nap robots?","Nap length varies regardless of what they change."],
["sleeptrain-1xbwq0s","19rgehw6ria5h","partner","regression_4_months","desire",["bedtime_battle","marriage_strain"],"Yeah I would loooove his bedtime to be consistent so I can do chores and hang with my wife for a bit before bed.","What a consistent bedtime would buy the father."],
["sleeptrain-1xbwsys","","parent_unspecified","regression_4_months","belief",["ferber","comparison_other_babies","social_media_pressure"],"I see so many encouraging stories that go like: “first night cried for 25 minutes, then 10 minutes, then 2 minutes.” 3 days and poof it’s great","Success stories set the expectation her Ferber attempt failed against."],
["sleeptrain-1xbwsys","","parent_unspecified","regression_4_months","failure_story",["ferber","consistency_failure"],"First night 50 minutes, second night 30 minutes with a false start 20 minutes later, third night 50 minutes with a false start and inconsolable so we just called it.","Ferber attempt at 4.5 months abandoned after three nights."],
["sleeptrain-1xbwsys","","parent_unspecified","regression_4_months","fear",["ferber","retraining_after_setback"],"I want to attempt again but I’m scared. Did anyone have success but it took longer than 3 days and 25 minutes of crying?","Asks for slower success stories before retrying."],
["sleeptrain-1xbwsys","19rgmgpv9mp37","parent_unspecified","regression_4_months","regret",["ferber","consistency_failure"],"I think my expectations might’ve been a little skewed and it worried me something was wrong. I didn’t want to make it worse but I feel like that’s what I ended up doing 🤦🏻‍♀️","After hearing longer success stories."],
["sleeptrain-1xbwsys","19rh57o1n6v0g","parent_unspecified","regression_4_months","pain",["night_wakings","maternal_exhaustion"],"My problem is that his sleep is still so bad. Like, I’m dying. He goes down around 7:30, false start maybe 30 minutes later. Down again, sleeps until maybe 1:30? But then is up every 60-90 minutes after that. I really can’t live like this for 2 more months.","Told to wait a few weeks before retrying Ferber."],
["sleeptrain-1xbxndj","","experienced_mother","toddler_24_36_months","pain",["night_wakings","partner_split_nights","parent_work_impact"],"I’m the one that does all the night wakings and have done since he was born. I’m a stay at home mum and my husband works to he can’t be up all hours of the night","Two-year-old waking 4-6 times a night, breastfed back to sleep."],
["sleeptrain-1xbxndj","","experienced_mother","toddler_24_36_months","tried_failed",["night_weaning","vomiting_stop","cry_it_out"],"He goes absolutely crazy when I try and cries so much that he makes himself sick. This previously happened when we tried to sleep train.","Why night weaning and sleep training stopped."],
["sleeptrain-1xbxndj","","experienced_mother","toddler_24_36_months","pain",["guilt","maternal_exhaustion"],"I feel like I’m failing as a mother and I’m stuck in the endless sleep deprived cycle. I’m sorry for the long post but please be kind.","Two years of broken nights."],
["daddit-1xby2bj","","partner","toddler_24_36_months","regret",["dream_feed","night_weaning","parent_identity"],"tonight is the first night in my 2 year olds life where he doesn't get any sort of milk during the night. I was still \"dream feeding\" him a small amount around 11pm every single night, and loved doing that.","Father grieving the end of the dream feed he gave his toddler."],
["daddit-1xby2bj","","partner","toddler_24_36_months","belief",["dream_feed","parent_identity"],"I think I was doing this these past couple of months more for me than for him.","Father on why he kept the dream feed."],
["Parenting-1xby662","","experienced_mother","toddler_12_24_months","pain",["sleep_props","retraining_after_setback"],"Before the baby was born, he was sleeping through the night, and now it feels like we've taken a huge step backward.","Toddler of 21 months now needs rocking after new sibling arrived."],
["Parenting-1xby662","","experienced_mother","toddler_12_24_months","others_said",["relative_caregiver_conflict","sleep_props"],"My mother-in-law keeps telling me that it's impossible to get him to fall asleep without rocking him, especially at his age.","Breastfeeding mother of a newborn and a toddler."],
["Parenting-1xby662","","experienced_mother","toddler_12_24_months","pain",["room_sharing"],"We currently have only one bedroom available for the children and us, so I can't simply move my older son into another room.","Space limits shape every option."],
["Parenting-1xby662","","experienced_mother","toddler_12_24_months","question",["room_sharing","information_overload"],"I'm not looking for judgment or advice that assumes I can simply put him in his own bedroom, because that's not an option in our current living situation.","Pre-empting the usual replies."],
["Parenting-1xby662","19rg8dhrxszz4","experienced_mother","toddler_12_24_months","pain",["only_mum_settles","partner_split_nights"],"My husband is actually very involved and does everything he can to help. The problem is that my toddler only wants me. When his dad tries to comfort him, he screams","Defending her husband against commenters."],
["sleeptrain-1xbyctc","","experienced_mother","baby_9_12_months","trigger_moment",["retraining_after_setback","night_wakings","doctor"],"She's been sleep trained for 6 months. And it was perfect, 7pm bedtime without a fight, Asleep soundly until 7am. But late September she got really sick and ended up admitted for a few days.","Twelve-month-old waking nightly since a hospital stay."],
["sleeptrain-1xbyctc","","experienced_mother","baby_9_12_months","tried_failed",["ferber","success_story"],"When we sleep trained her (ferber) we realized us doing the check Ins were making things worse for her. […] So we modified what we were doing and would only check in when she really needed us, and she figured it out very quickly, like two days.","Their modified Ferber worked the first time."],
["sleeptrain-1xbyctc","","experienced_mother","baby_9_12_months","pain",["daycare_naps","parent_work_impact"],"She's also just started daycare so we have limited ability to control her napping. Anyway, this was long enough. Advice, your own experiences are welcome. Thank you -a tired mom that goes back to work soon 😔","Breastfeeding mother returning to work."],
["sleeptrain-1xbyctc","19rgko5ww78bo","experienced_mother","baby_9_12_months","others_said",["daycare"],"They gave us a slot earlier than we needed but you don't turn down a daycare slot.","Daycare start forced by slot availability."],
["sleeptrain-1xbyctc","19rhc63ci4rfo","experienced_mother","baby_9_12_months","success_story",["free_advice_wins","wake_windows","retraining_after_setback"],"I kept her up 30 min longer before bed and she had one wake. I did a check after she didn't settle on her own. And she fell back asleep on her own until 7 this morning. So maybe she needed some more awake time.","Commenters' sleep-budget advice tried the next night."],
["toddlers-1xbysx4","","parent_unspecified","toddler_24_36_months","pain",["night_wakings","drop_nap","doctor"],"She has night terrors or confessional arousal at 3/4am every single night. i’ve reached out to pediatrician but waiting on a response…..","Two-year-old fighting naps and waking screaming nightly."],
["Mommit-1xbyv8m","","new_mother","baby_9_12_months","fear",["ferber","guilt","cry_it_out"],"In the mornings, she used to wake up babbling and playing and smiling, but since starting sleep training, she wakes up crying in the morning. It’s been weighing on my mind because I’m worried she fell asleep sad which caused her to wake up sad.","Seven days into Ferber with an almost-1-year-old that is otherwise working."],
["Mommit-1xbyv8m","","new_mother","baby_9_12_months","trigger_moment",["bedtime_battle","sleep_props"],"I love the snuggle time with my baby, but an hour out of the day sometimes just ends in frustration so we decided to try the Ferber method.","Snuggling to sleep had stretched to an hour."],
["Mommit-1xbyv8m","19rg9p3x7vj5t","new_mother","baby_9_12_months","belief",["ferber","cry_it_out","sleep_training_values"],"We chose Ferber method because it allows for the check ins. We don’t do “cry it out”. I think people who just leave their babies for the night are insane.","Drawing her line between Ferber and CIO."],
["toddlers-1xbzigp","","experienced_mother","toddler_24_36_months","others_said",["drop_nap","partner_disagreement"],"My husband took him on a walk when he got home and he fell asleep in the stroller. So he was tired. My husband told me I need to take him on a walk when he doesn't go down for a nap.","Twenty-five-month-old stopped napping."],
["toddlers-1xbzigp","","experienced_mother","toddler_24_36_months","pain",["drop_nap","parent_work_impact","maternal_exhaustion"],"His nap used to be so dependable and I was counting on it to get work done for my part time job but now I don't get any reprieve whatsoever during the day.","Lost nap means lost work time."],
["toddlers-1xbzigp","","experienced_mother","toddler_24_36_months","pain",["guilt"],"something definitely is bothering him but I just feel like I am failing and not meeting his needs somehow.","Nap refusal plus picky eating."],
["beyondthebump-1xc1jox","","parent_unspecified","baby_5_8_months","pain",["sleep_props","conflicting_advice","sleep_training_values"],"I’m so tired of hearing the reason he can’t resettle himself is because he needs the same thing he went to sleep with (rocking, nursing, whatever) if I don’t help him to sleep he will just cry and cry and cry. He needs the support I’m not looking for sleep training advice, just venting.","Seven-month-old; every nap and bedtime a battle."],
["beyondthebump-1xc1jox","","parent_unspecified","baby_5_8_months","pain",["comparison_other_babies","guilt"],"I feel like I’m doing something wrong because all my friends have babies that sleep well and/or just put themselves to sleep. Like did I screw up my babies nervous system by being stressed or the times I freaked out while he was crying uncontrollably???","Blames herself for her baby's sleep."],
["beyondthebump-1xc1jox","19rhdb16av2qq","parent_unspecified","baby_5_8_months","tried_failed",["wake_windows"],"I’ve tweaked his wake windows so many times though. Shorter, longer, less naps, more naps it all is the same result.","Replying to a wake window suggestion."],
["beyondthebump-1xc1jox","19rhevpby39nn","parent_unspecified","baby_5_8_months","question",["wake_windows","short_naps"],"There are times when he fight sleep so bad I am pretty sure he’s under tired, but I don’t understand how he could be chronically under tired when he gets so little sleep during the day.","The undertired/overtired puzzle at 7 months."],
["beyondthebump-1xc1lvf","","new_mother","baby_5_8_months","pain",["contact_naps","feeding_to_sleep"],"She WILL NOT allow herself to sleep horizontally. It’s carrier or nothing","Eight-month-old fighting naps after first fever; mother pumping."],
["NewParents-1xc25fw","","parent_unspecified","newborn_0_8_weeks","pain",["conflicting_advice","information_overload","sleep_training_values"],"New parent here and feeling totally overwhelmed by all the conflicting info I’m getting on newborn sleep. It seems like there are two camps.","Newborn parent caught between independence and attachment camps."],
["NewParents-1xc25fw","","parent_unspecified","newborn_0_8_weeks","objection",["course_purchase","conflicting_advice","social_media_pressure"],"The one thing they have in common is they all want me to buy their online course!🙄","On both sleep camps online."],
["NewParents-1xc25fw","","parent_unspecified","newborn_0_8_weeks","desire",["gentle_method","schedule_rigidity","travel_disruption"],"I’m not a homebody and we like to travel so we don’t want to be too rigid. […] But I want him to get good sleep and be able to sleep independently. Is there some sort of middle ground here?","Wants a balance between the two camps."]
